[0.488, "o", "\u001b[?25h"]
[0.021, "o", "\r\n# Case: decision-leads-with-point  with 1  without 0.6666666666666666\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "## with the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "We decided to store eval records as one JSON file per run, organized under `evals/`.\r\n\r\nSQLite requires building and maintaining a schema migration tool. Postgres requires running a database server. JSON files generate clean diffs in code review, which lets reviewers spot exactly what changed.\r\n\r\nOne question stays open: how long we keep old records. We need to settle a retention policy.\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## without the rune\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "Hi,\r\n\r\nI wanted to follow up on the storage approach for eval records that we discussed today.\r\n\r\nWe looked at three options: SQLite, Postgres, and one JSON file per run. We went with JSON files because they're simpler to set up (no migration tool or running server needed) and they show up cleanly in code review diffs. We'll store them under `evals/<run>/records/`.\r\n\r\nOne thing we didn't settle on yet is how long we should keep old records. We should figure that out soon.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "\r\n# Case: one-question-at-a-time  with 0.8333333333333334  without 0.5\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## with the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "To recommend the right backup solution, I need to understand your setup. Let me start with the most important question:\r\n\r\n**Where do you want your backups stored?** For instance: an external hard drive connected to your laptop, a cloud service like iCloud or Backblaze, both, or somewhere else entirely?\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## without the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "Good question to ask first. Here's what would help me recommend a backup strategy for you:\r\n\r\n1. **Operating system**: What's your laptop running (macOS, Windows, Linux)?\r\n2. **What needs backing up**: Everything, or just specific files/folders (docs, photos, code, etc.)?\r\n3. **How much data**: Roughly how much total (e.g., 100 GB, 500 GB, 2 TB)?\r\n4. **Local, cloud, or both**: Do you want backups stored locally (external drive), in the cloud, or a combination?\r\n5. **Recovery speed**: How quickly do you need to restore if something breaks?\r\n6. **Budget**: Any cost constraints, or willing to pay for a service?\r\n7. **Existing setup**: Are you currently backing up anything, or starting from scratch?\r\n8. **Frequency**: How often should backups happen (daily, weekly)?\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "Even just answering a few of these would let me point you toward something practical.\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "\r\n# Case: status-update-abbreviations  with 0.3333333333333333  without 0.20000000000000004\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "## with the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "The CDN TTL change we made at 01:30 breached the p99 TTFB SLO for 40 minutes. We rolled back the TTL at 02:10 and latency recovered.\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## without the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "**Incident Status Update**\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "A CDN TTL configuration change deployed at 01:30 UTC caused our p99 TTFB SLO to be breached for 40 minutes. We identified the issue, rolled back the TTL at 02:10 UTC, and latency recovered to normal levels. No customer-facing impact beyond the SLO window.\r\n"]
[0.139, "x", "0"]
